1
00:00:02,653 --> 00:00:06,123
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:14,131 --> 00:00:16,400
Okay, this is getting real.

3
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,200
I'm being tracked.

4
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,239
So, my options are to either keep
the suit on or else strip down.

5
00:00:22,273 --> 00:00:24,074
I don't mind walking around naked,

6
00:00:24,074 --> 00:00:26,710
but I do mind bullets.

7
00:00:26,744 --> 00:00:30,147
If I keep the suit on, I'll still
have people trying to kill me

8
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:32,516
...which, I'm kind of used to anyway...

9
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:35,219
But if I take it off and I get shot,

10
00:00:35,219 --> 00:00:36,253
then, that's it.

11
00:00:36,287 --> 00:00:37,521
I'm fucked.

12
00:00:37,554 --> 00:00:39,156
You know what I'm saying, man?

13
00:00:39,156 --> 00:00:40,157
You should!

14
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:41,725
You don't even have a weapon!

15
00:00:41,725 --> 00:00:43,527
And don't think I'm
going to give you one.

16
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:46,430
Well, I'm not stripping in front of you,
in case you're wondering.

17
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:49,099
There's too many damned
people in this building.

18
00:00:49,099 --> 00:00:51,168
Woah-ho...drafty.

19
00:00:51,168 --> 00:00:52,169
Okay...

20
00:00:52,202 --> 00:00:53,904
Oh, my god, it's cold in here!

21
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:56,807
IS THIS 10 FUCKING KELVIN?!

22
00:00:56,807 --> 00:00:57,441
[shivering, muttering]
Don't get locked...

23
00:00:57,441 --> 00:00:58,442
[shivering, muttering]
Don't get locked out in the open...

24
00:00:58,442 --> 00:01:08,819
[shivering, muttering]

25
00:01:08,819 --> 00:01:09,820
[shivering, muttering]
....okayokayokaywarmwarmwarm...

26
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:13,557
...okayokaywarmwarmpipes, warm pipes...

27
00:01:13,557 --> 00:01:14,892
....warm pipes good.

28
00:01:14,892 --> 00:01:16,093
Warm pipes...

29
00:01:16,093 --> 00:01:18,362
Oh...ooh...

30
00:01:18,362 --> 00:01:19,663
Frosty.

31
00:01:21,265 --> 00:01:23,400
Well, I was wrong about one thing:

32
00:01:23,434 --> 00:01:26,737
Those aliens are NOT from a swamp planet.

33
00:01:26,737 --> 00:01:28,005
Anything that can--

34
00:01:28,005 --> 00:01:29,773
Oh, my god.

35
00:01:29,773 --> 00:01:31,842
This whole neighborhood's going to hell.

36
00:01:31,842 --> 00:01:33,043
What, with the gangs...

37
00:01:33,043 --> 00:01:34,478
[vortigaunt attack]

38
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:34,912
Yep...

39
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,984
Can't even walk down the street
of your own planet anymore!

40
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:41,919
I remember the good old days, when

41
00:01:41,919 --> 00:01:44,154
I didn't have to bring a gun to work,

42
00:01:44,154 --> 00:01:46,590
my coworkers weren't space bugs,

43
00:01:46,623 --> 00:01:48,292
I had a salary,

44
00:01:48,292 --> 00:01:50,694
I wasn't wanted by the government,

45
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:51,695
then YOU happened!

46
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:53,697
Ow!

47
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:54,765
Was I shot in the back of the--

48
00:01:54,765 --> 00:01:56,767
[vortigese]

49
00:01:57,434 --> 00:02:00,237
No respect, man.  No respect at all.

50
00:02:00,237 --> 00:02:02,906
God damned outworlders
are ruining this country.

51
00:02:02,906 --> 00:02:06,010
There was a time when
we'd put you all in cages.

52
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:08,612
And, if it was up to me,
it'd still be that way.

53
00:02:08,645 --> 00:02:11,181
Some of you keep
zapping me with electricity.

54
00:02:11,181 --> 00:02:13,083
That means you're a power source.

55
00:02:13,083 --> 00:02:15,152
We should be taking advantage of that.

56
00:02:15,152 --> 00:02:16,620
This is all so wasted.

57
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:17,354
Guard: Freeman, right?

58
00:02:17,388 --> 00:02:18,055
Yeah?

59
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:19,056
Guard: I got a message for you.

60
00:02:19,056 --> 00:02:20,090
Guard: Make sure you don't--

61
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:21,091
[gunshot]
Guard: Augh...

62
00:02:21,091 --> 00:02:21,625
Daah!

63
00:02:21,625 --> 00:02:22,826
Okay!  10-4!

64
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:24,061
I'll be sure not to do that!

65
00:02:25,095 --> 00:02:29,266
Eh, my intuition tells me
that wasn't the full message.

66
00:02:29,266 --> 00:02:32,736
Something about him killing himself
to make a point doesn't add up.

67
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:35,339
That, and the silenced gunshot
makes me think

68
00:02:35,339 --> 00:02:37,641
there's something devious going on here.

69
00:02:37,674 --> 00:02:38,642
Ah-hah!

70
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:39,476
Hm.

71
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:40,911
I don't see anyone.

72
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,813
Maybe the problem went away.

73
00:02:42,813 --> 00:02:45,082
Maybe I willed it out of existence.

74
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:47,718
Maybe it was the magical
sniper fairy that comes and gives

75
00:02:47,718 --> 00:02:51,288
silenced hollow-point rounds to
people who don't eat their vegetables.

76
00:02:51,288 --> 00:02:53,123
That was one of the Grimm's Tales, right?

77
00:02:53,123 --> 00:02:54,491
[gunshots]
Ah, ah, ah!

78
00:02:55,993 --> 00:02:56,960
Ninjas!

79
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,762
These aren't fairies!  They're ninjas!

80
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:02,566
[gunshots]

81
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:03,667
Okay, move, move, move!

82
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:06,737
In order to beat a ninja,
I have to think like a ninja!

83
00:03:06,737 --> 00:03:08,672
[gunshots]

84
00:03:08,705 --> 00:03:09,573
Flank, flank, flank!

85
00:03:09,706 --> 00:03:10,040
Double back!

86
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:11,942
[gunshots]

87
00:03:11,942 --> 00:03:14,311
I trace electron orbits!
You think I can't find you?

88
00:03:14,311 --> 00:03:15,779
[gunshots]

89
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:16,880
Fucking ninjas, man.

90
00:03:17,581 --> 00:03:19,316
Oh ho!  Ninja in the closet.

91
00:03:19,349 --> 00:03:20,517
Ninja in the closet!

92
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:22,086
Oh, some ammo.

93
00:03:22,086 --> 00:03:23,554
Yeah, I think I'll take that.

94
00:03:24,054 --> 00:03:25,589
Ninjas, man.

95
00:03:25,589 --> 00:03:27,925
I was not ready for ninjas.

96
00:03:27,925 --> 00:03:29,493
Who IS ready for ninjas?

97
00:03:29,493 --> 00:03:31,428
No one!  They're ninjas!

98
00:03:31,428 --> 00:03:34,064
I've never even seen a ninja until today.

99
00:03:34,064 --> 00:03:35,899
Except for that dude at the
knife store.

100
00:03:35,899 --> 00:03:37,234
They're probably already gone.

101
00:03:37,234 --> 00:03:38,435
Disappeared into smoke.

102
00:03:39,136 --> 00:03:40,337
Oh, nope.

103
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:41,605
Well, this settles it.

104
00:03:41,605 --> 00:03:44,408
Black Mesa is a
James Bond villain company.

105
00:03:44,408 --> 00:03:45,509
We have missiles,

106
00:03:45,509 --> 00:03:46,410
robots,

107
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:47,077
lasers,

108
00:03:47,077 --> 00:03:47,811
sharks,

109
00:03:47,811 --> 00:03:48,946
and ninjas.

110
00:03:48,946 --> 00:03:50,814
Ah!  "Surface Access"!

111
00:03:51,515 --> 00:03:53,083
[grunts]

112
00:03:53,083 --> 00:03:54,251
Dammit...

113
00:03:54,251 --> 00:03:56,787
Eh, maybe I'll level this place.

114
00:03:56,787 --> 00:04:00,057
Whoah!  Holy shit!

115
00:04:00,057 --> 00:04:01,959
It's morning.

116
00:04:01,959 --> 00:04:04,461
How did I not notice this?

117
00:04:04,461 --> 00:04:07,598
Man, I am tripping balls!

118
00:04:07,598 --> 00:04:10,200
Time is moving WAY too fast.

119
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,536
Something's wrong with my brain.

120
00:04:12,536 --> 00:04:15,739
It's like that experiment where they kept
that guy underground in a cave

121
00:04:15,772 --> 00:04:21,945
for a few weeks with no time reference,
and his body adjusted to a 25-hour cycle.

122
00:04:21,945 --> 00:04:22,646
Oh, here we go.

123
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:25,182
Except, in my case,
my body's waiting to go--

124
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:28,152
[grunts]

125
00:04:28,152 --> 00:04:30,854
Jesus Christ...

126
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,126
Hey, it opened!

127
00:04:36,126 --> 00:04:37,594
What was I thinking about?

128
00:04:37,594 --> 00:04:39,463
Oh, yeah, I need a watch.

129
00:04:39,463 --> 00:04:41,999
Eh, that's okay. Watches are cheap.

130
00:04:41,999 --> 00:04:43,834
So, what should I do about this suit?

131
00:04:43,834 --> 00:04:45,936
What, with the ninjas
tracking me and all.

132
00:04:45,936 --> 00:04:48,172
I'm starting to like how
it's painted bright orange.

133
00:04:48,172 --> 00:04:52,376
I think it makes people want to shoot me
in the torso instead of the head.

134
00:04:52,376 --> 00:04:54,678
So, should I take it off or leave it on?

135
00:04:54,678 --> 00:04:55,879
I don't know.

136
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:57,915
The stripper's dilemma.

137
00:04:57,915 --> 00:05:01,685
If I wasn't a fugitive, I could publish
a paper on this and get some money.

138
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:04,788
I'll wait and keep it on until I find
a car, then ditch it.

139
00:05:05,556 --> 00:05:06,323
HECU #1: Get him!

140
00:05:06,323 --> 00:05:07,324
No!  Cut it out!

141
00:05:07,324 --> 00:05:09,026
[punching]

142
00:05:09,026 --> 00:05:10,627
Urgh...

143
00:05:10,627 --> 00:05:12,796
HECU #1: Heh heh heh.  Nice hit.

144
00:05:23,207 --> 00:05:25,375
HECU #2: Where are we taking
this Freeman guy?

145
00:05:25,375 --> 00:05:27,177
HECU #1: Topside for questioning.

146
00:05:27,177 --> 00:05:29,379
HECU #2: What the hell for?  We got him.

147
00:05:29,379 --> 00:05:30,447
HECU #2: Let's kill him now!

148
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,014
No...

149
00:05:31,014 --> 00:05:33,283
HECU #1: Uh, and if they find the body?

150
00:05:33,283 --> 00:05:35,886
HECU #2: Body?  What body?

151
00:05:35,886 --> 00:05:37,821
HECU #1 and #2: (laughing)

152
00:05:37,821 --> 00:05:39,567
Ah hah hah hah hah hah hah...

